| P32 | First-run import returns to the wizard | A v1 import during first run commits its tenants through the reviewed C23 flow; the desktop then has a tenant, so the first-run draft ends (its credentials are cleaned up) and the shell opens on the imported tenant; its scan key is added in Administration (the reviewed C08/C09 credential setup) | A tenant that exists is never sent back through a first-run wizard (P30), and the wizard cannot wrap an existing tenant without duplicating it |
| P33 | `ReadStatus` as its own core scope with per-product states from dedicated reads | Derived in the core from the Runtime overview read the shell already owns: Runtime Security from the sessions chart and the key inventory, AI Gateway from the chosen workspace's usage and limits (not read when no workspace is chosen, and said so), Red Team and model/skill reads are `notRead` on Home (their destinations read them); partial sources are named; a completed read bumps a generation the presentation announces | No second read pipeline: Home never claims coverage a read did not establish (I4) |
| P34 | Inbox items with `kind`, `severity` and `explanation` per item | `InboxEntry` carries the overview item (Runtime, Gateway) or the C29 setup warning with its hold; the explanation is per kind in the presentation's copy, not invented per item; `deadline` is absent (P20) | The admitted reads report no per-item explanation or deadline |
